WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.291 --> 00:00:32.833
<b>In the previous verse, Lord Krishna explained</b>

2
00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:36.291
<b>that having renounced all attachments</b>
<b>to the fruits of their actions,</b>

3
00:00:36.291 --> 00:00:39.333
<b>a wise person remains ever </b>
<b>content and self-satisfied.</b>

4
00:00:39.333 --> 00:00:46.583
<b>They do not depend on any external object, </b>
<b>person, or circumstance for this contentment.</b>

5
00:00:46.583 --> 00:00:53.708
<b>The discussion here is about an individual </b>
<b>who is advanced on the path of Karma Yoga.</b>

6
00:00:53.708 --> 00:00:54.625
<b>Now,</b>

7
00:00:54.625 --> 00:00:57.666
<b>in this twenty-first verse of the fourth chapter,</b>

8
00:00:57.666 --> 00:01:00.541
<b>and also in the next twenty-second verse,</b>

9
00:01:00.541 --> 00:01:03.791
<b>the qualities and characteristics of such an </b>
<b>advanced person</b>

10
00:01:03.791 --> 00:01:06.458
<b>in Karma Yoga are being described.</b>

11
00:01:11.208 --> 00:01:12.875
<b>Within this verse,</b>

12
00:01:12.875 --> 00:01:13.791
<b>Lord Krishna</b>

13
00:01:13.791 --> 00:01:19.916
<b>has described four main qualities of an </b>
<b>advanced individual on the path of Karma Yoga.</b>

14
00:01:19.916 --> 00:01:21.000
<b>First quality -</b>

15
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.375
<b>Nirāśīḥ -</b>

16
00:01:22.375 --> 00:01:25.916
<b>meaning free from the desire for gain.</b>

17
00:01:25.916 --> 00:01:31.583
<b>A Karma Yogi performs their duties </b>
<b>without any desire for reward.</b>

18
00:01:31.583 --> 00:01:35.125
<b>They are not motivated by </b>
<b>the results of their actions.</b>

19
00:01:35.125 --> 00:01:39.583
<b>It is this selfless attitude that </b>
<b>purifies their every action.</b>

20
00:01:39.583 --> 00:01:42.125
<b>This is what liberates them,</b>

21
00:01:42.125 --> 00:01:45.708
<b>because one who renounces </b>
<b>concern for outcomes</b>

22
00:01:45.708 --> 00:01:49.708
<b>does not get entangled in the </b>
<b>cycle of actions and reactions.</b>

23
00:01:49.708 --> 00:01:51.125
<b>Second quality -</b>

24
00:01:51.125 --> 00:01:53.250
<b>Yata-cittātmā -</b>

25
00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:56.458
<b>meaning control over the mind and intellect.</b>

26
00:01:56.458 --> 00:01:59.833
<b>Such a person performs every </b>
<b>action with concentration,</b>

27
00:01:59.833 --> 00:02:02.250
<b>and while performing actions,</b>

28
00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:07.916
<b>focuses their attention only on </b>
<b>noble goals such as human welfare.</b>

29
00:02:07.916 --> 00:02:11.791
<b>No greed or desire misleads them.</b>

30
00:02:11.791 --> 00:02:15.458
<b>This is possible only due to control</b>
<b>over the mind and intellect.</b>

31
00:02:15.458 --> 00:02:19.666
<b>It is this discipline that keeps </b>
<b>them steady and balanced.</b>

32
00:02:19.666 --> 00:02:20.958
<b>Third quality -</b>

33
00:02:20.958 --> 00:02:23.125
<b>Tyakta-sarva-parigrahaḥ -</b>

34
00:02:23.125 --> 00:02:26.291
<b>meaning renunciation of </b>
<b>the sense of proprietorship.</b>

35
00:02:26.291 --> 00:02:30.208
<b>Such a person does not claim ownership </b>
<b>over any material object.</b>

36
00:02:30.208 --> 00:02:36.250
<b>They believe that ultimately this entire creation </b>
<b>belongs only to the Supreme Lord,</b>

37
00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:41.791
<b>so how can they have personal ownership </b>
<b>over any object in this creation?</b>

38
00:02:41.791 --> 00:02:46.250
<b>For this reason, they neither assert their </b>
<b>authority over material objects,</b>

39
00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:48.708
<b>nor do they become attached to them.</b>

40
00:02:48.708 --> 00:02:53.958
<b>It is this renunciation of attachment that </b>
<b>keeps them free from the bondage of actions.</b>

41
00:02:53.958 --> 00:02:55.583
<b>Fourth quality -</b>

42
00:02:55.583 --> 00:02:58.416
<b>Śārīraṁ kevalaṁ karma –</b>

43
00:02:58.416 --> 00:03:03.875
<b>meaning they only fulfill their </b>
<b>basic bodily necessities,</b>

44
00:03:03.875 --> 00:03:09.291
<b>so that the body remains active and </b>
<b>they can perform selfless actions.</b>

45
00:03:09.291 --> 00:03:14.833
<b>Such a person never indulges in unnecessary </b>
<b>activities of sense gratification.</b>

46
00:03:14.833 --> 00:03:18.875
<b>They keep their life simple and limit their needs.</b>

47
00:03:18.875 --> 00:03:22.291
<b>It is important to understand these four qualities.</b>

48
00:03:22.291 --> 00:03:25.000
<b>If you want to imagine such a person,</b>

49
00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:28.125
<b>you can take the example of a farmer.</b>

50
00:03:28.125 --> 00:03:32.666
<b>In this country, there are many</b>
<b>farmers who plow the fields,</b>

51
00:03:32.666 --> 00:03:39.666
<b>grow various crops, and then society arranges</b>
<b>its food from those very crops.</b>

52
00:03:39.666 --> 00:03:43.250
<b>That farmer grows many crops for others,</b>

53
00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:44.000
<b>but</b>

54
00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:46.625
<b>keeps his personal life simple.</b>

55
00:03:46.625 --> 00:03:51.000
<b>He only fulfills his basic bodily needs,</b>

56
00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:56.166
<b>so that he can remain healthy, work hard, </b>
<b>and do his duty.</b>

57
00:03:56.166 --> 00:03:59.750
<b>That farmer is content with little.</b>

58
00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:04.583
<b>Lord Krishna wants to convey that to </b>
<b>remain free from the bondage of actions,</b>

59
00:04:04.583 --> 00:04:06.958
<b>these four qualities are necessary –</b>

60
00:04:06.958 --> 00:04:09.833
<b>freedom from profit and desire,</b>

61
00:04:09.833 --> 00:04:12.458
<b>control over the mind and intellect,</b>

62
00:04:12.458 --> 00:04:15.583
<b>renunciation of the sense of </b>
<b>ownership and authority,</b>

63
00:04:15.583 --> 00:04:24.708
<b>and finally a simple life that only </b>
<b>fulfills basic bodily necessities.</b>

64
00:04:24.708 --> 00:04:31.541
<b>Such a life leads us towards inner </b>
<b>peace and spiritual liberation.</b>

65
00:04:36.208 --> 00:04:38.791
<b>Aparigraha -</b>

66
00:04:38.791 --> 00:04:43.875
<b>a crucial word in this verse,</b>

67
00:04:43.875 --> 00:04:49.125
<b>Which actually means renunciation of ownership.</b>

68
00:04:49.125 --> 00:04:57.333
<b>It means not claiming or asserting</b>
<b>your right over any object,</b>

69
00:04:57.333 --> 00:05:12.541
<b>be it a material possession, your skills, or even </b>
<b>your personal, social, or professional identity.</b>

70
00:05:12.541 --> 00:05:15.375
<b>You must understand,</b>

71
00:05:15.375 --> 00:05:25.000
<b>that claiming ownership over anything </b>
<b>in this universe is an illusion,</b>

72
00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:34.458
<b>for you don't truly own any of it.</b>

73
00:05:34.458 --> 00:05:38.125
<b>Relinquishing ownership and attachment</b>

74
00:05:38.125 --> 00:05:44.625
<b>reduces your preoccupation and</b>
<b>worry about the material world.</b>

75
00:05:44.625 --> 00:05:51.458
<b>Because when you stop considering anything </b>
<b>as yours,</b>

76
00:05:51.458 --> 00:05:56.291
<b>the fear of losing it no longer haunts you.</b>

77
00:05:56.291 --> 00:06:05.541
<b>Take your house, for example. Is it permanent?</b>

78
00:06:05.541 --> 00:06:07.541
<b>Is it truly yours?</b>

79
00:06:07.541 --> 00:06:11.250
<b>Can it not be taken away from you?</b>

80
00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:17.750
<b>And can it not be given back to you?</b>

81
00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:19.583
<b>Ponder this – </b>

82
00:06:19.583 --> 00:06:26.041
<b>when you entered this world, </b>
<b>this house wasn't yours,</b>

83
00:06:26.041 --> 00:06:28.333
<b>and when you depart,</b>

84
00:06:28.333 --> 00:06:32.416
<b>it still won't be yours.</b>

85
00:06:32.416 --> 00:06:37.583
<b>So where is the ownership and possession?</b>

86
00:06:37.583 --> 00:06:44.333
<b>Consider it a temporary shelter.</b>

87
00:06:44.333 --> 00:06:48.541
<b>Adopting this perspective will lessen your fears,</b>

88
00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:55.208
<b>allowing you to live a free and stress-free life.</b>

89
00:06:55.208 --> 00:06:59.916
<b>Consider your skills.</b>

90
00:06:59.916 --> 00:07:03.041
<b>Did you bring them with you at birth?</b>

91
00:07:03.041 --> 00:07:04.416
<b>No.</b>

92
00:07:04.416 --> 00:07:07.208
<b>What you gained, you gained here.</b>

93
00:07:07.208 --> 00:07:11.250
<b>And if you acquired these skills in this world,</b>

94
00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:17.166
<b>then use them for the welfare of the world.</b>

95
00:07:17.166 --> 00:07:23.916
<b>This mindset will protect you from envy </b>
<b>and inspire you to serve society.</b>

96
00:07:23.916 --> 00:07:25.750
<b>Your identity?</b>

97
00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:29.666
<b>Take your professional position, for instance.</b>

98
00:07:29.666 --> 00:07:31.041
<b>Think about it,</b>

99
00:07:31.041 --> 00:07:34.000
<b>Is it really yours?</b>

100
00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:40.625
<b>Or is it given to you merely</b>
<b>to facilitate your duties?</b>

101
00:07:40.625 --> 00:07:48.541
<b>This thought will reduce your ego and </b>
<b>save you from a life of stress and comparison</b>

102
00:07:48.541 --> 00:07:50.375
<b>Aparigraha -</b>

103
00:07:50.375 --> 00:07:53.708
<b>the renunciation of ownership and possession –</b>

104
00:07:53.708 --> 00:07:59.708

<b>to practice it, keep these four things in mind.</b>

105
00:07:59.708 --> 00:08:01.125
<b>First -</b>

106
00:08:01.125 --> 00:08:03.833
<b>Evaluation. </b>

107
00:08:03.833 --> 00:08:08.625
<b>Evaluate whatever you have.</b>

108
00:08:08.625 --> 00:08:09.541
<b>Think about it,</b>

109
00:08:09.541 --> 00:08:13.083
<b>are you attached to it?</b>

110
00:08:13.083 --> 00:08:17.875
<b>Does it aid in your spiritual growth?</b>

111
00:08:17.875 --> 00:08:25.208
<b>Or are you clinging to it merely out of </b>
<b>ownership and greed?</b>

112
00:08:25.208 --> 00:08:26.666
<b>Second -</b>

113
00:08:26.666 --> 00:08:28.083
<b>Detachment</b>

114
00:08:28.083 --> 00:08:29.708
<b>or Liberation.</b>

115
00:08:29.708 --> 00:08:36.041
<b>Try to donate some of the unnecessary </b>
<b>material possessions.</b>

116
00:08:36.041 --> 00:08:38.375
<b>Free yourself from them.</b>

117
00:08:38.375 --> 00:08:39.541
<b>Third -</b>

118
00:08:39.541 --> 00:08:41.125
<b>Generosity.</b>

119
00:08:41.125 --> 00:08:42.958
<b>Sharing with others.</b>

120
00:08:42.958 --> 00:08:46.291
<b>The things you need -</b>

121
00:08:46.291 --> 00:08:50.875
<b> a material object, your skills, etc.</b>

122
00:08:50.875 --> 00:08:52.291
<b>think about it,</b>

123
00:08:52.291 --> 00:09:00.000
<b>can they be shared? Can they </b>
<b>help someone else?</b>

124
00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.625
<b>And the fourth one -</b>

125
00:09:01.625 --> 00:09:03.208
<b>Gratitude</b>

126
00:09:03.208 --> 00:09:04.875
<b>and Mindfulness.</b>

127
00:09:04.875 --> 00:09:07.000
<b>Always be grateful,</b>

128
00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:10.375
<b>for you have received much.</b>

129
00:09:10.375 --> 00:09:13.375
<b>Whatever you received, you received here.</b>

130
00:09:13.375 --> 00:09:18.375
<b>And be mindful that this is not mere coincidence.</b>

131
00:09:18.375 --> 00:09:27.458
<b>Your life is part of a grand cosmic plan.</b>

132
00:09:27.458 --> 00:09:34.833
<b>And you must play your part with full dedication,</b>
<b>selflessness, and a spirit of service.</b>

133
00:09:34.833 --> 00:09:36.208
<b>Evaluation,</b>

134
00:09:36.208 --> 00:09:37.250
<b>Liberation,</b>

135
00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:38.333
<b>Generosity,</b>

136
00:09:38.333 --> 00:09:40.750
<b>Gratitude, and Mindfulness –</b>

137
00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:46.958
<b>adhering to these four principles is the </b>
<b>observance of Aparigraha.</b>

138
00:09:46.958 --> 00:09:50.500
<b>Apply them in your life.</b>

139
00:09:54.833 --> 00:09:57.708
<b>Now here let's understand</b>

140
00:09:57.708 --> 00:10:09.625
<b>how to practice Aparigraha, a key principle </b>
<b>from this verse, in a family setting.</b>

141
00:10:09.625 --> 00:10:13.916
<b>In the family context, Aparigraha means</b>

142
00:10:13.916 --> 00:10:25.666
<b>reducing the sense of ownership and possession </b>
<b>not only over objects but also relationships.</b>

143
00:10:25.666 --> 00:10:27.625
<b>Consider,</b>

144
00:10:27.625 --> 00:10:32.375
<b>which love or respect is sweeter?</b>

145
00:10:32.375 --> 00:10:38.250
<b>The love or respect you have to </b>
<b>demand by asserting your right,</b>

146
00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:45.166
<b>or the one that flows freely to you on its own?</b>

147
00:10:45.166 --> 00:10:57.166
<b>And if you have to assert your right </b>
<b>- then is it truly love at all?</b>

148
00:10:57.166 --> 00:10:59.833
<b>Now again imagine</b>

149
00:10:59.833 --> 00:11:08.666
<b>a family where everyone loves each other,</b>
<b>respects each other.</b>

150
00:11:08.666 --> 00:11:12.208
<b>Here, everyone gives,</b>

151
00:11:12.208 --> 00:11:13.708
<b>doesn't demand.</b>

152
00:11:13.708 --> 00:11:14.625
<b>And</b>

153
00:11:14.625 --> 00:11:21.708
<b>as a result, everyone now has an abundance</b>
<b>of love given by others.</b>

154
00:11:21.708 --> 00:11:26.500
<b>Now take an example of material objects –</b>

155
00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:30.125
<b>someone bought a vehicle in the house.</b>

156
00:11:30.125 --> 00:11:35.916
<b>Is it better to consider it personal </b>
<b>property and flaunt it,</b>

157
00:11:35.916 --> 00:11:40.666
<b>or to consider the vehicle as </b>
<b>belonging to everyone,</b>

158
00:11:40.666 --> 00:11:45.958
<b>so that family members can </b>
<b>use it for their commute?</b>

159
00:11:45.958 --> 00:11:49.875
<b>Here's another example of Aparigraha.</b>

160
00:11:49.875 --> 00:11:55.125
<b>If someone in the family progresses </b>
<b>or gets promoted,</b>

161
00:11:55.125 --> 00:12:02.875
<b>everyone is genuinely </b>
<b>happy about it, not envious.</b>

162
00:12:02.875 --> 00:12:06.333
<b>This too is the spirit of Aparigraha,</b>

163
00:12:06.333 --> 00:12:11.125
<b>where you believe that everyone </b>
<b>has a right to progress.</b>

164
00:12:11.125 --> 00:12:12.666
<b>Not just you,</b>

165
00:12:12.666 --> 00:12:16.041
<b>but everyone should advance.</b>

166
00:12:16.041 --> 00:12:24.208
<b>The feeling of Aparigraha can be cultivated</b>
<b>in the family through small practical measures –</b>

167
00:12:24.208 --> 00:12:25.666
<b>first,</b>

168
00:12:25.666 --> 00:12:28.208
<b>start with yourself.</b>

169
00:12:28.208 --> 00:12:31.541
<b>Share your things with others.</b>

170
00:12:31.541 --> 00:12:37.416
<b>Only if you practice it can you inspire others.</b>

171
00:12:37.416 --> 00:12:44.416
<b>Designate some time in the family when </b>
<b>everyone does someone else's work.</b>

172
00:12:44.416 --> 00:12:45.875
<b>For example,</b>

173
00:12:45.875 --> 00:12:50.458
<b>one day, the father and children</b>
<b>cook for the mother.</b>

174
00:12:50.458 --> 00:12:56.166
<b>This will increase the sense of </b>
<b>help and mutual respect.</b>

175
00:12:56.166 --> 00:13:01.541
<b>And yes, have regular conversations </b>
<b>about these principles.</b>

176
00:13:01.541 --> 00:13:06.958
<b>So that everyone knows that the </b>
<b>foundation of this family is love,</b>

177
00:13:06.958 --> 00:13:08.375
<b>a spirit of service,</b>

178
00:13:08.375 --> 00:13:10.583
<b>helping each other.</b>

179
00:13:10.583 --> 00:13:16.166
<b>In this family, everyone complements </b>
<b>and cooperates with each other.</b>

180
00:13:16.166 --> 00:13:19.833
<b>Everyone has a right to all things.</b>

181
00:13:19.833 --> 00:13:23.916
<b>How beautiful is the vision of such a family.</b>

182
00:13:23.916 --> 00:13:26.083
<b>Make it real.</b>

183
00:13:26.083 --> 00:13:31.083
<b>Take the first step towards Aparigraha today.</b>

184
00:13:35.458 --> 00:13:37.750
<b>Aparigraha -</b>

185
00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:40.125
<b>or the renunciation of ownership –</b>

186
00:13:40.125 --> 00:13:44.541
<b>is extremely important in a professional setting.</b>

187
00:13:44.541 --> 00:13:51.541
<b>This perspective teaches that you should </b>
<b>perform your duty with full dedication</b>

188
00:13:51.541 --> 00:13:52.333
<b>but</b>

189
00:13:52.333 --> 00:13:55.750
<b>not claim ownership over the results.</b>

190
00:13:55.750 --> 00:14:05.375
<b>At the same time, understand that you are </b>
<b>merely a custodian of a position, not its owner.</b>

191
00:14:05.375 --> 00:14:08.833
<b>Let's understand these two points.</b>

192
00:14:08.833 --> 00:14:12.333
<b>The outcome or professional achievement –</b>

193
00:14:12.333 --> 00:14:13.791
<b>think,</b>

194
00:14:13.791 --> 00:14:18.958
<b>do you really have full ownership of it?</b>

195
00:14:18.958 --> 00:14:21.916
<b>If the organization hadn't provided the facilities?</b>

196
00:14:21.916 --> 00:14:30.291
<b>If colleagues hadn't helped? If senior </b>
<b>officials hadn't provided guidance?</b>

197
00:14:30.291 --> 00:14:34.125
<b>Could you have done it all?</b>

198
00:14:34.125 --> 00:14:35.750
<b>No.</b>

199
00:14:35.750 --> 00:14:44.416
<b>In every achievement, like others, </b>
<b>you are merely making your contribution.</b>

200
00:14:44.416 --> 00:14:49.541
<b>You don't have complete ownership of it.</b>

201
00:14:49.541 --> 00:14:55.625
<b>This mindset will teach you gratitude, </b>
<b>cooperation, and a spirit of service.</b>

202
00:14:55.625 --> 00:15:00.541
<b>Take the example of your professional position – </b>

203
00:15:00.541 --> 00:15:06.250
<b>this position belonged to </b>
<b>someone else before you, </b>

204
00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:09.791
<b>and will belong to someone else after you.</b>

205
00:15:09.791 --> 00:15:11.041
<b>This position</b>

206
00:15:11.041 --> 00:15:14.958
<b>is given to you to fulfill your duties.</b>

207
00:15:14.958 --> 00:15:20.000
<b>So just make the performance </b>
<b>of your duty your goal,</b>

208
00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:22.375
<b>don't claim ownership over the position.</b>

209
00:15:22.375 --> 00:15:26.291
<b>A senior official who adopts this thinking</b>

210
00:15:26.291 --> 00:15:33.833
<b>will surely respect others and attribute </b>
<b>the organization's progress to everyone.</b>

211
00:15:33.833 --> 00:15:40.833
<b>As a result, he too will receive only </b>
<b>respect and cooperation.</b>

212
00:15:40.833 --> 00:15:42.625
<b>Moreover,</b>

213
00:15:42.625 --> 00:15:47.291
<b>here are two other benefits </b>
<b>of practicing Aparigraha:</b>

214
00:15:47.291 --> 00:15:48.708
<b>First:</b>

215
00:15:48.708 --> 00:15:51.041
<b>Your stress will reduce.</b>

216
00:15:51.041 --> 00:15:59.791
<b>If you don't own the position or progress, </b>
<b>then there will be no fear of losing it.</b>

217
00:15:59.791 --> 00:16:01.125
<b>Second:</b>

218
00:16:01.125 --> 00:16:05.791
<b>You will freely share your knowledge </b>
<b>and skills with others.</b>

219
00:16:05.791 --> 00:16:06.666
<b>Because</b>

220
00:16:06.666 --> 00:16:12.833
<b>if these skills have also been given to </b>
<b>you by the grace of God and mentors,</b>

221
00:16:12.833 --> 00:16:17.500
<b>then why hesitate in sharing them with others?</b>

222
00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:21.208
<b>This should be the mindset of an ideal employee.</b>

223
00:16:21.208 --> 00:16:26.166
<b>Especially when you are leading others.</b>

224
00:16:26.166 --> 00:16:27.875
<b>Reflect on it.</b>

225
00:16:27.875 --> 00:16:33.375
<b>And practice Aparigraha in a practical setting too.</b>

